WEBVTT

00:04.220 --> 00:06.770
K-Kazuki-kun...

00:07.320 --> 00:11.740
Attacks he can't perceive
aren't reflected right away.

00:11.740 --> 00:16.540
So, all we need to do is to make him
unable to say "reflect" with an attack.

00:16.540 --> 00:17.960
Is that what you thought?

00:19.500 --> 00:23.590
It has nothing to do with
my vision or my perception.

00:23.920 --> 00:27.260
It's not automatic.
I decide what attacks to reflect.

00:27.630 --> 00:31.970
I purposely didn't reflect
the attack on my back.

00:31.970 --> 00:35.100
I don't even need to say
"reflect" for it to work.

00:36.210 --> 00:39.440
No one has ever injured me...

00:40.030 --> 00:41.270
and no one ever will.

00:48.490 --> 00:52.030
I had faith in the two of you...

00:52.030 --> 00:53.700
but I guess not.

01:02.500 --> 01:04.750
Usato-kun...

01:04.750 --> 01:06.850
I'm... sorry.

01:22.520 --> 01:27.190
THE WRONG WAY TO USE HEALING MAGIC

02:38.010 --> 02:39.890
#11 SMASH! FIST OF HEALING!

02:39.890 --> 02:43.270
We managed to get those
school rules amended, didn't we?

02:43.640 --> 02:44.940
Excellent job, Senpai.

02:45.310 --> 02:48.770
No, it was thanks to your materials,
Kazuki-kun.

02:48.770 --> 02:50.360
You really are dependable.

02:50.360 --> 02:51.900
No, no.

02:51.900 --> 02:54.650
Just from the teachers
you were talking with,

02:54.650 --> 02:58.780
I could really see the respect
and expectations they had for you.

02:58.780 --> 03:00.350
That is why we succeeded.

03:03.040 --> 03:04.210
You think so?

03:04.210 --> 03:05.060
Of course!

03:06.090 --> 03:07.710
Oh, I'm sorry.

03:07.710 --> 03:08.960
I'll go grab my bag.

03:08.960 --> 03:10.630
Sure, I'll make my way down first.

03:13.720 --> 03:16.140
Respect and expectations, huh?

03:21.140 --> 03:22.750
It's not stopping!

03:25.770 --> 03:26.700
Oh?

03:28.560 --> 03:29.630
I'm really glad...

03:30.190 --> 03:32.510
I met you that day.

03:33.570 --> 03:36.360
When I was summoned
to another world,

03:36.680 --> 03:37.760
I was so happy.

03:38.360 --> 03:41.330
I could finally be a new me.

03:41.330 --> 03:42.910
That is all I could think about.

03:44.000 --> 03:47.210
But... you were different.

03:48.150 --> 03:51.340
You did everything you could
to prepare yourself

03:51.340 --> 03:54.420
for living a new life in a new world.

03:54.960 --> 03:56.590
You were so dazzling,

03:57.030 --> 03:58.550
I could hardly look at you.

03:59.760 --> 04:01.370
And on top of that,

04:01.950 --> 04:05.050
when you accepted not the old me,
which was just a facade,

04:05.680 --> 04:10.020
but the real me that could finally
emerge in this new world...

04:10.020 --> 04:11.390
I was really happy.

04:12.270 --> 04:15.280
As long as I had you
and Kazuki-kun by my side,

04:15.650 --> 04:17.110
everything would be all right...

04:17.110 --> 04:19.070
...or so I thought.

04:19.070 --> 04:20.200
However...

04:25.450 --> 04:26.870
Our Heroes!

04:27.190 --> 04:29.040
Praise the Black Knight!

04:30.460 --> 04:31.960
We did it!

04:39.880 --> 04:41.720
Time to end this.

04:44.990 --> 04:46.560
That was fun...

04:46.560 --> 04:48.100
for a little while.

04:56.610 --> 05:02.530
No you don't!

05:07.950 --> 05:09.620
Kazuki! Senpai!

05:11.610 --> 05:12.790
I didn't make it!

05:15.130 --> 05:17.210
No, I did make it!

05:26.680 --> 05:29.600
Usato-kun...

05:32.000 --> 05:33.190
Senpai!

05:39.690 --> 05:41.870
That hurt!

05:43.280 --> 05:45.080
What was that?

05:46.870 --> 05:48.870
Who are you?!

05:57.900 --> 05:58.920
Time to run!

06:01.170 --> 06:02.220
Not on your life!

06:12.560 --> 06:14.850
Senpai! You're all healed up?

06:15.480 --> 06:17.290
Yeah! Thanks!

06:17.980 --> 06:20.440
I'm just about done
healing Kazuki's wounds.

06:20.440 --> 06:22.470
He should wake up soon.

06:22.900 --> 06:26.280
I see...
Listen to this, Usato-kun.

06:26.280 --> 06:27.170
Incoming!

06:33.750 --> 06:35.370
That was close!

06:35.370 --> 06:39.840
Come on... I still have those
other knights to heal, you know?

06:39.840 --> 06:42.420
Listen, Usato-kun.

06:42.420 --> 06:46.340
Your attack on the Black Knight worked!

06:47.180 --> 06:48.760
What do you mean?

06:48.760 --> 06:52.180
His armor is most likely made of magic.

06:52.180 --> 06:55.900
It reflects all attacks
back on the attacker.

06:56.980 --> 06:59.860
Are you serious?
That's totally cheating.

06:59.860 --> 07:03.280
But your punch worked!

07:03.280 --> 07:05.360
What was that attack?

07:05.360 --> 07:07.310
That attack?

07:09.330 --> 07:11.330
I won't let you escape.

07:11.330 --> 07:13.800
I don't know what that was,

07:14.370 --> 07:18.410
but I'm going to have to
pay you back for that.

07:19.750 --> 07:22.380
I honestly don't want to fight.

07:22.380 --> 07:25.420
But I can't save everyone
with him around.

07:26.230 --> 07:27.110
So be it!

07:31.310 --> 07:32.390
Usato-kun?

07:32.390 --> 07:34.600
You two stay here.

07:35.140 --> 07:37.190
I'll hold him off.

07:42.230 --> 07:44.150
Come! To your death!

07:45.240 --> 07:46.700
Careful, Usato-kun!

07:47.660 --> 07:49.370
Morphing at will?

07:49.370 --> 07:51.490
But even if my attacks are reflected,

07:51.490 --> 07:52.950
I can heal myself!

07:57.500 --> 07:59.380
My attacks aren't being reflected?

07:59.380 --> 08:00.500
Is he out of mana?

08:02.170 --> 08:03.460
How?

08:03.880 --> 08:05.090
He's taken aback!

08:05.090 --> 08:06.260
In that case...

08:07.050 --> 08:08.260
Take this!

08:11.390 --> 08:14.720
Sorry! That was a feint!

08:19.730 --> 08:21.440
Why you...

08:22.860 --> 08:25.070
Die!

08:25.820 --> 08:28.950
I'm not going to
just because you said so!

08:33.409 --> 08:35.289
Usato...

08:35.610 --> 08:37.500
Kazuki-kun, you're awake!

08:37.960 --> 08:39.580
What happened?

08:40.539 --> 08:42.960
Did Usato heal me?

08:44.300 --> 08:46.960
He saved both of our lives.

08:46.960 --> 08:48.170
And he's now...

08:49.880 --> 08:51.720
fighting the Black Knight.

08:53.140 --> 08:54.970
Oh, no!

08:55.890 --> 08:57.640
Now what?

09:01.440 --> 09:03.480
What's happening?

09:03.480 --> 09:07.070
The Black Knight's attacks
aren't having any effect.

09:07.860 --> 09:13.700
For some reason, Usato-kun's
attacks aren't being reflected.

09:15.120 --> 09:19.750
Also, why is Usato cloaking himself
in healing magic?

09:19.750 --> 09:22.960
He isn't healing his own
wounds or fatigue, right?

09:22.960 --> 09:24.170
Yeah...

09:24.170 --> 09:27.250
He's just healing the enemy
every time he lands a hit...

09:29.630 --> 09:30.670
Don't tell me...

09:30.670 --> 09:32.800
the Black Knight's weakness is...

09:33.340 --> 09:34.470
healing magic?

09:39.350 --> 09:41.730
Magic that activates
when the user is injured

09:42.100 --> 09:45.190
can't activate when the attack
is cloaked in healing magic.

09:45.900 --> 09:48.120
That's because the injury
that should be reflected

09:48.120 --> 09:50.150
has already been healed!

09:50.150 --> 09:51.070
That means...

09:51.070 --> 09:53.820
the only thing hurting
the Black Knight is...

09:55.320 --> 09:56.990
...nothing but...

09:56.990 --> 09:58.660
Usato-kun's punches!

09:59.620 --> 10:01.580
They don't leave any injuries,

10:01.580 --> 10:03.000
but they hurt like hell!

10:07.960 --> 10:09.460
That's so messed up!

10:13.840 --> 10:14.800
That's...

10:15.820 --> 10:19.060
That's the wrong way to use healing magic!

10:21.770 --> 10:22.800
You're kidding me.

10:24.100 --> 10:25.730
This can't be happening.

10:26.860 --> 10:28.320
Not to me!

10:37.700 --> 10:38.830
You..

10:38.830 --> 10:41.750
I'll kill you!

10:41.750 --> 10:42.960
Usato!

10:43.410 --> 10:44.290
Kazuki!

10:44.290 --> 10:45.420
You're awake!

10:45.420 --> 10:46.130
Thank goodness!

10:46.920 --> 10:47.880
Usato-kun!

10:48.590 --> 10:50.230
No need to worry!

10:51.340 --> 10:53.050
I'll take him out in one more hit.

10:53.370 --> 10:54.380
Take him out?

10:54.380 --> 10:58.180
No matter what magic he uses,

10:58.800 --> 11:00.810
it doesn't change what I have to do.

11:01.310 --> 11:02.600
Make sure...

11:02.890 --> 11:05.440
he doesn't hurt anyone else...

11:05.730 --> 11:06.940
ever again!

12:15.260 --> 12:16.580
I nailed it.

12:18.130 --> 12:19.590
That was the killing move...

12:19.590 --> 12:21.600
No, the winning move...

12:22.390 --> 12:23.810
The healing punch.

12:31.900 --> 12:32.690
There we go.

12:32.690 --> 12:34.320
Everything's fine now.

12:34.320 --> 12:35.780
Thank you so much.

12:35.780 --> 12:37.820
Thank you for saving us.

12:38.220 --> 12:38.940
Not at all.

12:40.780 --> 12:43.490
It's all in a day's work
for the Rescue Squad.

12:43.490 --> 12:45.660
Not just for healing us,

12:45.660 --> 12:48.460
but for beating the Black Knight

12:48.460 --> 12:50.870
and for making the demons
lose their will to fight.

12:51.920 --> 12:53.920
That's right, Usato-kun.

12:53.920 --> 12:55.800
If you hadn't beaten the Black Knight,

12:55.800 --> 12:57.930
there would have been
many more casualties.

12:59.170 --> 13:00.800
I guess you're right.

13:00.800 --> 13:02.260
I am indeed.

13:02.260 --> 13:03.680
Good job to you, too.

13:03.680 --> 13:05.180
You can go get some rest.

13:05.180 --> 13:06.770
Thank you, ma'am.
Right away.

13:09.730 --> 13:11.230
Usato-kun,

13:11.230 --> 13:13.310
you really saved the day.

13:13.310 --> 13:14.520
You were amazing.

13:15.440 --> 13:16.360
Nah...

13:16.360 --> 13:19.030
So... about that healing punch?

13:19.030 --> 13:20.700
You heard that?

13:20.700 --> 13:23.870
EXCITED EXCITED
That was a really interesting name.

13:23.870 --> 13:25.870
EXCITED EXCITED
What kind of move was that?

13:25.870 --> 13:28.600
Well, it's not anything special.

13:29.290 --> 13:31.620
It's just my fist
cloaked in healing magic.

13:31.980 --> 13:33.230
That's all there is to it.

13:34.290 --> 13:36.420
The captain taught it to me.

13:36.920 --> 13:40.670
I've got a special technique
for idiots like you.

13:41.880 --> 13:45.640
Listen up because I'm only
going to say this once.

13:46.260 --> 13:50.060
If you face an enemy you have to
defeat no matter what...

13:50.390 --> 13:53.190
Punch 'em with a fist
full of healing magic.

13:54.060 --> 13:56.070
Heal them as you hit them.

13:56.070 --> 13:58.280
That way, you won't kill them.

13:58.280 --> 14:00.040
You'll just knock them out.

14:00.940 --> 14:04.660
Even without the damage,
they'll still feel the pain and impact.

14:04.660 --> 14:08.120
With this, I can knock them out
without leaving any lasting injuries!

14:08.120 --> 14:10.330
Amazing, isn't it?

14:10.330 --> 14:11.790
Y-Yup.

14:11.790 --> 14:14.210
You're corrupted, all right...

14:15.170 --> 14:16.420
by Rose-san.

14:16.880 --> 14:18.420
Stop that!

14:18.420 --> 14:20.010
Please don't lump us together!

14:21.880 --> 14:23.590
Well, to be fair...

14:23.590 --> 14:28.970
it is a fact that that healing punch
saved the two of us.

14:29.670 --> 14:30.660
You have my thanks.

14:33.560 --> 14:36.190
No thanks necessary.

14:36.190 --> 14:38.610
You're my precious senpai,

14:38.610 --> 14:40.730
and Kazuki is my dear friend.

14:43.400 --> 14:44.910
Senpai!

14:45.160 --> 14:48.830
That snake monster has
moved to the front lines.

14:49.110 --> 14:49.870
I see.

14:49.870 --> 14:52.040
Then that's what we're fighting next.

14:52.040 --> 14:52.910
Right!

14:52.910 --> 14:55.290
Then I'll head to the front lines
with you guys.

14:55.870 --> 14:56.870
Hey!

14:57.790 --> 14:59.380
C-Captain!

14:59.380 --> 15:02.460
I heard that the Heroes
were on the verge of death.

15:02.810 --> 15:04.470
What's going on?

15:04.470 --> 15:05.970
Explain the situation.

15:06.390 --> 15:08.850
W-Well, you see...

15:09.390 --> 15:12.770
Right... so that's the Black Knight.

15:13.640 --> 15:16.690
To think that you'd be the one
to put an end to everything.

15:16.690 --> 15:17.900
I'm sorry...

15:17.900 --> 15:19.690
Don't be.

15:19.690 --> 15:22.780
Healing the Heroes,
capturing a powerful enemy combatant,

15:22.780 --> 15:24.700
and sending their forces into disarray.

15:25.400 --> 15:26.410
Now's a good time.

15:27.490 --> 15:30.120
We're heading back to camp.

15:30.120 --> 15:30.990
Excuse me?

15:31.360 --> 15:33.450
The battle has swung heavily in our favor.

15:33.450 --> 15:36.170
As long as they don't have
anything up their sleeve,

15:36.170 --> 15:37.880
we've got this in the bag.

15:37.880 --> 15:41.090
We're just going to get in the way.

15:44.880 --> 15:46.510
Kazuki, Senpai!

15:46.510 --> 15:48.840
I'm heading back with the captain.

15:48.840 --> 15:50.390
I see...

15:50.390 --> 15:51.470
Thanks for the heads up.

15:51.470 --> 15:53.600
I can't thank you enough, Usato.

15:53.600 --> 15:56.060
Don't die on me now.

15:56.060 --> 16:00.270
You guys are the Heroes!
Go kick their butts!

16:00.270 --> 16:01.480
You got it.

16:01.480 --> 16:04.860
I'm not going to waste
the life you gave me.

16:05.280 --> 16:06.280
Usato.

16:09.620 --> 16:10.450
See ya!

16:15.580 --> 16:17.710
Good job staying alive.

16:18.120 --> 16:20.170
Sorry, did you say something?

16:20.170 --> 16:21.720
Nothing. Let's book it.

16:22.380 --> 16:23.630
Right behind you!

16:25.050 --> 16:28.180
The Black Knight... got captured?

16:28.480 --> 16:30.590
According to those who were there,

16:30.590 --> 16:33.600
it was a one-sided battle.

16:33.970 --> 16:37.680
Impossible! Her magic was beaten?

16:38.390 --> 16:39.520
Was it a Hero?

16:39.520 --> 16:42.400
No, it was someone in white.

16:42.400 --> 16:45.730
Most likely one of the Rescue Squad.

16:45.730 --> 16:46.780
Was it Rose?

16:46.780 --> 16:49.570
No, it was a black-haired boy.

16:50.780 --> 16:52.820
There was... another one?

16:56.080 --> 16:58.790
Hyriluk, call Baljinak back.

16:59.750 --> 17:00.710
We're falling back.

17:01.210 --> 17:02.790
Are you serious?

17:02.790 --> 17:05.250
I should join the battle,

17:05.250 --> 17:08.220
but I won't be able to protect
the base with just the soldiers.

17:08.540 --> 17:12.180
Not to mention, they still have
Army Commander Siglis on their side.

17:12.970 --> 17:14.470
Any more fighting...

17:14.470 --> 17:15.760
would be pointless.

17:15.760 --> 17:18.390
We don't have any healers,

17:18.390 --> 17:20.480
so it's just a matter of time.

17:20.480 --> 17:23.050
All right.
I'll issue the order.

17:24.650 --> 17:25.730
What's wrong?

17:26.819 --> 17:27.930
It's the Heroes.

17:28.650 --> 17:32.070
Time to show them what we're made of.

17:32.070 --> 17:32.860
Right.

17:32.860 --> 17:36.080
Let's kick this guy's butt and go home!

17:37.290 --> 17:38.410
Let's do this!

18:00.310 --> 18:02.690
Usato! No slacking!

18:02.690 --> 18:05.110
Shut up! I'm not slacking!

18:07.020 --> 18:09.400
He got poisoned.
You know what to do.

18:09.400 --> 18:10.440
Got it!

18:10.440 --> 18:11.830
I'll heal you now.

18:24.290 --> 18:26.630
We did it, Senpai!

18:26.630 --> 18:29.670
Yup! You really are dependable!

18:37.760 --> 18:39.100
It's all over!

18:39.100 --> 18:41.020
Please take it easy for now.

18:41.600 --> 18:43.770
G-Got it.

18:43.770 --> 18:45.060
Thanks.

18:45.060 --> 18:47.610
No, thank you for making it back alive!

18:48.480 --> 18:50.570
Looks like we've won this battle.

18:51.190 --> 18:52.650
Are you serious?!

18:52.650 --> 18:55.860
They've begun to retreat.

18:55.860 --> 18:57.490
We're not giving chase?

18:57.490 --> 18:58.660
Are you crazy?

18:58.660 --> 19:01.620
Compared to them, we've spent
far more energy and resources.

19:01.620 --> 19:05.170
We should avoid unnecessary sacrifices
and prepare for the next attack.

19:05.870 --> 19:08.290
There'll be another one?

19:08.290 --> 19:11.010
Don't see why there won't be.

19:12.260 --> 19:14.880
Usato! We need you over here!

19:15.590 --> 19:16.180
Coming!

19:16.180 --> 19:17.390
I got it.

19:18.800 --> 19:19.600
Thanks.

19:23.730 --> 19:25.390
We were only able to win this battle

19:25.390 --> 19:29.560
because you were able
to revive the Heroes.

19:30.860 --> 19:34.030
You would have saved them
even if I wasn't here.

19:34.030 --> 19:35.820
They would have been saved regardless.

19:35.820 --> 19:36.630
No.

19:37.110 --> 19:39.590
They would have died.

19:41.030 --> 19:42.790
You saved them.

19:42.790 --> 19:45.370
Not Siglis. Not me.

19:45.370 --> 19:46.620
Got it?

19:46.620 --> 19:50.960
Without you,
we wouldn't have won so quickly.

19:50.960 --> 19:54.300
There was a chance
we might have even lost.

19:54.880 --> 19:59.220
You have done your job
as a member of the Rescue Squad.

20:01.390 --> 20:04.140
Well done, Usato.

20:45.270 --> 20:47.630
Huh? Why am I...?

20:50.690 --> 20:51.610
Look at you.

20:51.610 --> 20:54.570
You're crying like a kid!

20:54.570 --> 20:57.550
Duh! I'm still 17!

20:59.530 --> 21:02.990
The battle was really scary,

21:02.990 --> 21:04.490
and so were the demons!

21:05.580 --> 21:07.930
I saw many people die.

21:08.660 --> 21:09.410
But...

21:10.460 --> 21:11.430
But...

21:12.080 --> 21:13.450
I'm so happy to have met you...

21:14.500 --> 21:15.960
and to have been of help.

21:15.960 --> 21:17.130
I really am.

21:24.800 --> 21:28.390
Someone said the same thing to me once.

21:29.180 --> 21:32.520
Now, they're just a part of my memory.

21:33.900 --> 21:36.820
But you're here,
right in front of me.

21:37.860 --> 21:38.860
Usato...

21:39.990 --> 21:42.240
Thank you for making it back alive.

21:44.370 --> 21:45.370
My pleasure!

21:48.370 --> 21:49.500
Huh?

21:56.750 --> 21:59.260
No more magic or stamina, huh?

22:02.180 --> 22:04.090
You really hung in there.

22:04.090 --> 22:06.720
Now, rest.
